--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Bundled runtime (Windows installer only)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Windows Setup executable built by packaging/windows/build.ps1 embeds the
following in addition to the Python packages above. The Debian package
(packaging/debian/build_deb.py) does not embed any of these; it declares
python3, python3-tk and ffmpeg as dependencies resolved by the distribution.

  Python                    3.12+    PSF License (PSF-2.0)
    Copyright (c) 2001 Python Software Foundation. All rights reserved.
    Copyright (c) 2000 BeOpen.com. All rights reserved.
    Copyright (c) 1995-2001 Corporation for National Research Initiatives.
    Copyright (c) 1991-1995 Stichting Mathematisch Centrum, Amsterdam.
    https://www.python.org/ - full text: https://docs.python.org/3/license.html

  Tcl/Tk                             Tcl/Tk License (BSD-style)
    Copyright (c) Regents of the University of California, Sun Microsystems,
    Inc., Scriptics Corporation, ActiveState Corporation and other parties.
    Used by the launcher and the setup wizard through the standard-library
    tkinter module.
    https://www.tcl.tk/software/tcltk/license.html

  FFmpeg (ffmpeg.exe, ffprobe.exe)   GPL-3.0-or-later
    Copyright (c) 2000-2026 the FFmpeg developers.
    https://ffmpeg.org/
    The bundled binaries are the "essentials" release build from
    https://www.gyan.dev/ffmpeg/builds/ (downloaded by
    packaging/windows/fetch_ffmpeg.py). That build is compiled with GPL
    components (x264, x265 and others) and is therefore licensed as a whole
    under the GNU General Public License version 3. The license text ships
    alongside the binaries as tools/LICENSE-ffmpeg.txt.

    Touchdown Analyzer invokes ffmpeg and ffprobe as separate processes
    over their command-line interface; it does not link against FFmpeg's
    libraries and contains no FFmpeg code. Only the FFmpeg binaries are
    subject to the GPL; the Touchdown Analyzer code remains under the MIT
    License. The complete corresponding source for the bundled build is
    published by the build's maintainer at https://www.gyan.dev/ffmpeg/builds/
    and by the FFmpeg project at https://ffmpeg.org/download.html.

  PyInstaller bootloader    6.22.3   GPL-2.0-or-later with the PyInstaller
                                     Bootloader Exception
    Copyright (c) 2010-2026, PyInstaller Development Team.
    Copyright (c) 2005-2009, Giovanni Bajo.
    https://pyinstaller.org/
    The bootloader is embedded in every executable PyInstaller produces.
    Its license exception expressly permits distributing the resulting
    executable under any license, including the MIT License used here.
    Runtime hooks copied into the bundle are under the Apache License 2.0.
    Full text: https://github.com/pyinstaller/pyinstaller/blob/develop/COPYING.txt


